---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Storage Manager Privacy Policy - LogicPath Systems">
    <section class="legal-page" style="padding-top: 120px; min-height: 100vh;">
        <div class="container reveal">
            <div class="glass-card" style="padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);">
                <header style="margin-bottom: 3rem; text-align: center;">
                    <h1 class="gradient-text">Privacy Policy</h1>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;"><strong>Storage Manager</strong></p>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);"><strong>Last updated:</strong> 21 October 2026</p>
                </header>

                <main class="legal-content">
                    <h2>In short</h2>
                    <p>Storage Manager shows what is using space on your phone and helps you free some up. It works without an account. Your files and the list of your files stay on your phone. We do not collect, store or sell your personal data. The app uses Google Firebase Analytics to see which screens are used, and Google AdMob to show ads; both collect some device data as described below.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Permissions and why they are needed</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>All files access (MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE):</strong> the core of the app is managing the phone's storage. It needs this to analyse every folder (space by category, largest files and folders, duplicates, old files), to clean up (delete files you choose), and to let you browse, rename, copy and move files. It is requested only after an explanation, and you can turn it off at any time in Android settings.</li>
                        <li><strong>Usage access (PACKAGE_USAGE_STATS, optional):</strong> only if you allow it from the Apps screen. It shows each app's data and cache size and when you last used it. This is read on your phone and never sent anywhere. You can turn it off at any time in Android settings.</li>
                        <li><strong>Notifications (optional):</strong> only if you turn on the weekly storage check in Settings.</li>
                        <li><strong>Internet and network state:</strong> used only to load ads and send anonymous usage statistics. Your files are never uploaded.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Your files</h2>
                    <p>To show the storage analysis, the app keeps a list of file names, folders, sizes, types and dates, plus a daily total of used space for the storage trend chart, in a private database inside the app on your phone. It is never sent to us or anyone else. Uninstalling the app deletes it.</p>
                    <p>To find similar photos, the app makes a small fingerprint of each photo on your phone and keeps it in the same private database. Photos are never uploaded.</p>
                    <p>When you compress photos, each one is saved again at a smaller size in the same place, keeping its date and camera details (such as location, if the photo has it). The original goes to the Recycle bin for 7 days.</p>
                    <p>Files are opened, shared, exported or deleted only when you choose to. Deleted files are kept for 7 days in a hidden Recycle bin folder on your phone, then removed. Storage reports you export are saved to your Download folder.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Usage statistics (Firebase Analytics)</h2>
                    <p>The app uses Google Firebase Analytics to understand how it is used, so we can improve it. It records which screens you open (for example "Largest files" or "Settings"), app opens, how long sessions last, crashes of the analytics library itself, and basic device information: device model, Android version, app version, language, country (from your IP address) and an app-instance ID. Firebase may also use your advertising ID.</p>
                    <p>No file names, folder names, file contents, photos or search text are ever sent. Statistics are not linked to your name or any account.</p>
                    <p>Google keeps this data for up to 14 months and processes it on our behalf. How Google uses it: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a> and <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy</a></p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Advertising</h2>
                    <p>The app shows ads from Google AdMob: a banner on the Storage tab, an occasional full-screen ad after an analysis or clean-up you started, a full-screen ad that may appear when you come back to the app from another app (at most once every few minutes), and optional ads you can choose to watch to unlock extras. To show and measure ads, Google may collect your device's advertising ID, IP address, approximate location, device and app information, and how you interact with ads.</p>
                    <p>In the European Economic Area, the UK and Switzerland you are asked for consent first, and you can change your choice at any time in Settings → Privacy choices. You can also reset or delete your advertising ID in Android settings.</p>
                    <p>How Google uses this data: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a></p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Data sharing and security</h2>
                    <p>Usage statistics and ad data are sent only to Google (Firebase and AdMob) over an encrypted connection. We do not sell data or share it with anyone else.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Children</h2>
                    <p>The app is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect data from them.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
                    <p>We hold no data that identifies you. To remove everything the app stored on your phone, uninstall it or clear its storage in Android settings. Resetting your advertising ID in Android settings also stops new statistics and ad data being linked to earlier ones.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
                    <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be published in the app and on its web page with a new date.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 4rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);" />

                    <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2rem;">Disclaimer</h2>
                    <p>Storage Manager is an independent app. It is not made by or affiliated with Google or Android.</p>
                    <p>Deleted files go to the Recycle bin and are removed for good after 7 days, or straight away when you empty the bin. Files deleted in other apps or from a computer are not kept.</p>
                    <p>Storage figures and clean-up suggestions are estimates based on the last analysis. Decide yourself what is safe to remove.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Contact</h2>
                    <p><a href="mailto:contact@logicpathsystems.com" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">contact@logicpathsystems.com</a></p>
                </main>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layout>

<style>
    .legal-content h2 {
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
        font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .legal-content h3 {
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin-top: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
        font-size: 1.25rem;
    }

    .legal-content p, .legal-content ul {
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .legal-content ul {
        padding-left: 2rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .legal-content li {
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }
</style>
